    "title": "Woman killed, man injured in Stockton drive-by shooting days after mass attack - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Aidin Vaziri ,\n11 hours ago Two people were hospitalized after a drive-by shooting in Stockton on Tuesday, days after a mass shooting killed four. (San Joaquin County Sheriff’s Office) One person was killed and another injured Tuesday evening in a drive-by shooting in Stockton, according to the San Joaquin County Sheriff’s Office .\nDeputies responded just after 7 p.m. to the intersection of Gertrude Avenue and Fremont Street, where both victims were found with gunshot wounds and transported to a local hospital.\nThe woman later died from her injuries, and officials have not disclosed the man’s condition.\nTheir identities have not yet been released.\nWitnesses told KCRA that a man and a woman were struck, and others reported hearing about 10 gunshots. Investigators have not announced any arrests or identified a suspect vehicle.\nThe shooting comes only days after a mass shooting at a toddler’s birthday party in Stockton that left three children and a 21-year-old man dead and 13 others injured.\nAuthorities said it was too early to know whether the incidents are connected.\nSign up for San Francisco Chronicle newsletters here\nRead the original article on sfchronicle.com",
